if_iwxvar.h: the device configurations the header defines are static
(docs/tessronos/09-network.md 9.6.9).

Why: the header defines the objects of the cards' configurations
(const struct iwx_device_cfg iwx_..._cfg = { ... }), which only
if_iwx.c uses. TessronOS's layer includes the header in a second file
(device/net/wifi/obsd/tsw_iwx.c, for the layout of struct iwx_softc),
and each object would then be defined twice at the link. Static, each
file has its own, and if_iwx.c's are what it uses as before.

Applied by tools/openbsd/build.sh to a copy of the header, which is
found before OpenBSD's (-I); OpenBSD's tree is not changed.

